{
  "title": "70: al-Ma-a'arij المعارج",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nسَاَلَ سَآئِلٌ ۢ بِعَذَابٍ وَّاقِعٍۙ‏(1)\n\nDemanded, a demander, the chastisement inevitable\nلِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ لَيْسَ لَهٗ دَافِعٌ ۙ‏(2)\n\nFor the disbelievers against it, there is no repeller\nمِّنَ اللّٰهِ ذِى الْمَعَارِجِؕ‏(3)\n\nFrom God, the Lord of the Ways of Ascent\nتَعْرُجُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ وَ الرُّوْحُ اِلَيْهِ فِىْ يَوْمٍ كَانَ مِقْدَارُهٗ خَمْسِيْنَ اَلْفَ سَنَةٍ‌ۚ‏(4)\n\nUnto Him ascend the angels and the spirit in a day of the measure of fifty thousand years\nفَاصْبِرْ صَبْرًا جَمِيْلًا‏(5)\n\nSo be thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) patient with an excellent patience\nاِنَّهُمْ يَرَوْنَهٗ بَعِيْدًا ۙ‏(6)\n\nVerily, they regard it to be far distant\nوَّنَرٰٮهُ قَرِيْبًا ؕ‏(7)\n\nAnd we see (very) near\nيَوْمَ تَكُوْنُ السَّمَآءُ كَالْمُهْلِۙ‏(8)\n\nOn the Day the heaven shall be like molten brass\nوَتَكُوْنُ الْجِبَالُ كَالْعِهْنِۙ‏(9)\n\nAnd the mountain shall be as (flakes of) wool\nوَلَا يَسْئَلُ حَمِيْمٌ حَمِيْمًا ۖۚ‏(10)\n\nAnd will enquire not a friend of (his) friend\nيُّبَصَّرُوْنَهُمْ‌ؕ يَوَدُّ الْمُجْرِمُ لَوْ يَفْتَدِىْ مِنْ عَذَابِ يَوْمِئِذٍۢ بِبَنِيْهِۙ‏(11)\n\n(Though) they will be given sight of each other; The guilty one would fain redeem himself from the punishment of that Day at the price of his (own) children\nوَ صَاحِبَتِهٖ وَاَخِيْهِۙ‏(12)\n\nAnd his wife and his brother\nوَفَصِيْلَتِهِ الَّتِىْ تُئْوِيْهِۙ‏(13)\n\nAnd his kindred who gave him shelter\nوَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا ۙ ثُمَّ يُنْجِيْهِۙ‏(14)\n\nAnd all that are in the earth, (if) then that deliver him\nكَلَّاؕ اِنَّهَا لَظٰىۙ‏(15)\n\nBy no means! Verily, it is the flaming (Hell) fire\nنَزَّاعَةً لِّلشَّوٰى‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(16)\n\nDragging by the scalp\nتَدْعُوْا مَنْ اَدْبَرَ وَتَوَلّٰىۙ‏(17)\n\nClaiming him who turned his back and went away (from the Truth)\nوَجَمَعَ فَاَوْعٰى‏(18)\n\nAnd amassed (wealth), and shut it up\nاِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ خُلِقَ هَلُوْعًا ۙ‏(19)\n\nVerily man is created avaricious\nاِذَا مَسَّهُ الشَّرُّ جَزُوْعًا ۙ‏(20)\n\nWhen afflicteth him any evil, he is fretful\nوَاِذَا مَسَّهُ الْخَيْرُ مَنُوْعًا ۙ‏(21)\n\nWhen reacheth him any good, he is niggardly\nاِلَّا الْمُصَلِّيْنَۙ‏(22)\n\nSave those who offer (the regular) prayers\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَلٰى صَلَاتِهِمْ دَآئِمُوْنَۙ‏(23)\n\nThose who are ever constant at their prayers\nوَالَّذِيْنَ فِىْۤ اَمْوَالِهِمْ حَقٌّ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(24)\n\nAnd those in whose wealth is (realized) the right declared (by Us)\nلِّلسَّآئِلِ وَالْمَحْرُوْمِۙ‏(25)\n\nFor him who asketh and him who is prevented (by shame to ask)\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُصَدِّقُوْنَ بِيَوْمِ الدِّيْنِۙ‏(26)\n\nAnd those who testify the truth about the day of Judgment\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ مِّنْ عَذَابِ رَبِّهِمْ مُّشْفِقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(27)\n\nAnd those who are afraid of the chastisement of their Lord\nاِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّهِمْ غَيْرُ مَاْمُوْنٍ‏(28)\n\nVerily, the chastisement of their Lord is not to be felt secure of\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِفُرُوْجِهِمْ حٰفِظُوْنَۙ‏(29)\n\nAnd those who guard their private parts\nاِلَّا عَلٰٓى اَزْوَاجِهِمْ اَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُهُمْ فَاِنَّهُمْ غَيْرُ مَلُوْمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(30)\n\nSave unto their wives or those whom their right hands possess for then verily they are not to be blamed\nفَمَنِ ابْتَغٰى وَرَآءَ ذٰلِكَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْعٰدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(31)\n\nBut whoso seeketh beyond this, these are they who are the transgressors\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِاَمٰنٰتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رٰعُوْنَ ۙ‏(32)\n\nAnd those who, unto their pledges and covenants, are faithful\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِشَهٰدٰتِهِمْ قَآئِمُوْنَ ۙ‏(33)\n\nAnd those who in their testimonies are firm\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَلٰى صَلَاتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُوْنَؕ‏(34)\n\nAnd those who, at their (regular) prayers careful\nاُولٰٓئِكَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ مُّكْرَمُوْنَؕ‏(35)\n\nThose shall be in the gardens, (duly) honoured\nفَمَالِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا قِبَلَكَ مُهْطِعِيْنَۙ‏(36)\n\nBut what hath happened unto the disbelievers that they hasten on around you\nعَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ وَعَنِ الشِّمَالِ عِزِيْنَ‏(37)\n\nOn the right hand and on the left hand, in groups?\nاَيَطْمَعُ كُلُّ امْرِىءٍ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ يُّدْخَلَ جَنَّةَ نَعِيْمٍۙ‏(38)\n\nWhat! Coveteth every man of them to enter the Garden of Bliss?\nكَلَّا ؕ اِنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُمْ مِّمَّا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(39)\n\nBy no means! for We have created them of (the base matter) what they know!\nفَلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِرَبِّ الْمَشٰرِقِ وَالْمَغٰرِبِ اِنَّا لَقٰدِرُوْنَۙ‏(40)\n\nBut nay! I swear by the Lord of the Easts and the Wests, (that) We are certainly able\nعَلٰٓى اَنْ نُّبَدِّلَ خَيْرًا مِّنْهُمْۙ وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَسْبُوْقِيْنَ‏(41)\n\nTo substitute (in their stead) better ones than them, and We shall not be overtaken\nفَذَرْهُمْ يَخُوْضُوْا وَيَلْعَبُوْا حَتّٰى يُلٰقُوْا يَوْمَهُمُ الَّذِىْ يُوْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(42)\n\nSo thou leave them (to themselves) to remain in discoursing (in falsehood), and in (vanity) sporting, until they come face to face on the Day which has been promised (unto them)\nيَوْمَ يَخْرُجُوْنَ مِنَ الْاَجْدَاثِ سِرَاعًا كَاَنَّهُمْ اِلٰى نُصُبٍ يُّوْفِضُوْنَۙ‏(43)\n\nOn that Day they shall come forth from their graves in haste, as if they were hastening unto a signpost\nخَاشِعَةً اَبْصَارُهُمْ تَرْهَقُهُمْ ذِلَّةٌ ؕ ذٰلِكَ الْيَوْمُ الَّذِىْ كَانُوْا يُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(44)\n\nWith their eyes cast down, disgrace covering them; That is the Day which they were promised!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Ma-a’arij (The Ways of Ascent)\nThis Surah has 44 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting this Surah is equivalent to the total number of people who keep up prayer and safeguard the property which has been entrusted to them.\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that the one who recites this Surah will have his sins hidden on the Day of Judgement and he will enter Jannah alongside the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.). If a prisoner recites this Surah, he will secure his release. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that if this Surah is recited before sleeping, one keeps safe from the temptations of Shaitan."
